  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only the task-level search_object, approach_object, search_zone, and approach_zone movement events, the three claim and publication events, pickup and drop events, and the observations needed to select and complete the matching color branch. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because obstacle avoidance is already enforced by collision_avoidance, which protects these task-level movement actions.",
    "transition_design": "Each color becomes claimable only after its object-visible observation enters the corresponding claim-attempt state. A matching received_claim event abandons that attempt. A successful claim immediately enables repeated approach_object behavior, while object-not-visible observations return to claimed-object search. pick_up_object is enabled only after the matching object-reached observation. Pickup confirmation selects the same-color zone branch; repeated search_zone and approach_zone actions maintain movement, and zone-not-visible observations return to zone search. drop_object is enabled only after the matching zone-reached observation. Failures return to a recoverable search phase, successful delivery is published, and all branches terminate at delivery_complete, where no second delivery can start.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
